      "value": "I'm not opposed.\n\nI'm guessing you're referencing vmfunc's report back in Feburary. Tell me if there's any update since then.\n\nTo my understanding (please go read the original posts), no, it did NOT reveal such evidence that actual personal information was stolen from Persona. Instead, it explains how they discovered *strange* codes being public. In a later update, Persona CEO showed up and stated the codes were unused.\n\nSo, are they evil? None of us knows. \n\nShould you trust Persona? Probably no. However, VRChat team is basically 'trusting Persona so far'.\n\nI think Age Verification itself is a privacy nightmare by concept. I do not want it anywhere online. Because it all comes down to where they ask you to put your trust. It's funny that even such *safety* companies are doing the exact opposite of what we learned in school: Do not share your personal information online.\n\nJust think that no company has cared about privacy for ages.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
